onal support in renal insufficiency.", "LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO:Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo is a medical professional associated with CIDOS, focusing on nutritional support in renal insufficiency.", "MARÍA DEL PILAR SERRANO AGUAYO:Dr. María del Pilar Serrano Aguayo is a medical professional specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition. She is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation. Dr. Serrano Aguayo works at the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen del Rocío in Sevilla, where she applies her expertise to enhance the health and well-being of her patients.", "JOSÉ MANUEL SOUSA MARTÍN:Dr. José Manuel Sousa Martín is a medical professional specializing in the Digestive System, particularly within the Hepatic Transplant Unit at Hospital Universitario Virgen del Rocío in Sevilla. He is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation.", "CARMEN SENDRA FERNÁNDEZ:Carmen Sendra Fernández is a Resident Physician specializing in the Digestive System at the Hospital Universitario Virgen del Rocío in Sevilla. In her role, Dr. Sendra Fernández is actively involved in providing nutritional support for patients with chronic liver disease and those undergoing liver transplantation, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care in this critical area of medicine.", "ANA M. GÓMEZ PÉREZ:Ana M. Gómez Pérez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quirón-salud in Málaga. She is a medical professional who focuses on nutritional support for celiac disease and gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in managing dietary needs related to these conditions.", "ROSARIO FERNÁNDEZ GARCÍA-SALAZAR:Dr. Rosario Fernández García-Salazar is a medical professional specializing in Endocrinology and Clinical Nutrition at Hospital Quirón-salud in Málaga. She is particularly involved in providing nutritional support for celiac disease and managing gluten-controlled diets, demonstrating her expertise in addressing dietary needs related to these conditions.", "LUIS MIGUEL LUENGO PÉREZ:Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo Pérez is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders and is actively involved in research and practice related to nutritional support in metabolic disorders. He is associated with the Unidad de Nutrición Clínica y Dietética at Hospital Universitario Infanta Cristina, where he focuses on clinical nutrition and dietetics.", "ANA M. MÁRQUEZ ARMENTEROS:Dr. Ana M. Márquez Armenteros is a medical professional involved in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders.", "PILAR JIMÉNEZ NACIMIENTO:Dr. Pilar Jiménez Nacimiento is a medical professional specializing in nutritional support for amino acid metabolism disorders. She is affiliated with the Departamento de Ciencias Biomédicas at the Universidad de Extremadura, where she contributes to the field of biomedical sciences.", "HOSPITAL DE PONIENTE:Hospital de Poniente is a medical facility located in El Ejido, Almería, where Dr. Juan Pedro Rodríguez Rodríguez is a resident in internal medicine.", "ENFERMEDAD CELIACA:Celiac disease, known as \"enfermedad celíaca,\" is a chronic autoimmune disorder that primarily affects the small intestine. It is triggered by the ingestion of gluten in genetically predisposed individuals, leading to inflammation and damage to the intestinal mucosa. This condition results in malabsorption of nutrients, which can manifest through various gastrointestinal and extraintestinal symptoms. \n\nCeliac disease is characterized by the atrophy of the intestinal villi, particularly impacting nutrient absorption, especially in children. To manage the disease and prevent adverse reactions, individuals diagnosed with celiac disease must adhere to a strict gluten-free diet. This dietary restriction is essential to avoid further damage to the small intestine and to correct nutritional deficiencies that may arise from the condition. Overall, celiac disease is a significant health concern that requires careful management and lifestyle adjustments to ensure the well-being of affected individuals.", "METABOLISMOS DE LOS AMINOÁCIDOS:Amino acid metabolism disorders involve the body's inability to properly process amino acids, requiring specialized nutritional support."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}